# Production builds must never carry a key.
#
# Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the client bundle as a string literal,
# so a key present at build time is readable by anyone who loads the deployed
# site — "View source" is enough. Vite loads .env for every mode, which means a
# local .env used for development would otherwise end up in `npm run build`.
#
# This file loads after .env for mode=production and blanks the variable, so a
# production build is clean whatever is in .env. The app then asks each visitor
# for their own key and keeps it in their browser, which is the intended flow.
#
# Do not set VITE_NVIDIA_API_KEY here, or in Netlify's environment variables.
VITE_NVIDIA_API_KEY=
